---
/**
 * TODO: placeholder terms of service. Replace with the reviewed legal text
 * (and the registered entity name/address) before launch.
 */
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { site } from '../data/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Terms of service"
  description="Terms of service for the EZ Order Printer Shopify app and the ezorder.io website."
  lastUpdated="28 September 2026"
>
  <p class="not-prose rounded-xl border border-dashed border-line-strong bg-surface-muted p-4 text-sm text-muted">
    These terms are a working draft and will be replaced by the final terms of service.
  </p>

  <h2>1. The service</h2>
  <p>
    {site.name} (“the App”) is a Shopify application that generates, prints, downloads and emails
    order documents using data from your Shopify store. These terms apply to the App and to the
    ezorder.io website.
  </p>

  <h2>2. Your account</h2>
  <p>
    You use the App through your Shopify store. You are responsible for the content of your templates,
    for the accuracy of the business and tax details you add to documents, and for complying with the
    invoicing rules that apply to your business.
  </p>

  <h2>3. Plans and billing</h2>
  <p>
    The App is currently free. Any paid plan will be billed through Shopify, shown before you approve
    it, and can be cancelled by uninstalling the App.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Acceptable use</h2>
  <p>
    Do not use the App to send unsolicited email, to impersonate others, or in breach of Shopify's
    terms or applicable law.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Data</h2>
  <p>
    How we handle data is described in the <a href={site.privacyPolicyUrl}>app privacy policy</a>.
  </p>

  <h2>6. Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>
    We may update these terms and will note the date above. Questions:
    <a href={`mailto:${site.supportEmail}`}>{site.supportEmail}</a>.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
